Janis Papanagnou wrote:
...
> I think that score makes primarily sense for beginners to have some
> indication how they proceed and evolve. At the latest if you ascend
> on a regular basis the score becomes uninteresting
...

This does seem to be the general agreement.

The main reason we kept the score-based trophies is that it just seems 
wrong to entirely ignore the games own scoring mechanism; in deference 
to the consensus that score isn't the best way of measuring proficiency, 
we labeled those the _minor_ trophies.

We would certainly like to add a trophy (like Best Behaved, i.e. most 
monster races extinct) for most-extinctionist, which someone suggested 
earlier in this thread;  in our devnotes that prospective trophy is 
called Armageddon, but a better name is probably possible.  ;-)

I've learned a lot about patching NetHack this year, but I'd be happier 
if we could talk aardvark into expanding the xlog patch to include the 
things we'd need, so it could be generally available (rather than just a 
part of our bulk patch).  Monster races extinct, as a number field, 
shouldn't be a big addition to that patch.

As for point values, the Best in Show is intended to reflect a Clan's 
winnings in _all_ categories of trophy so it'd be inappropriate for it 
to ignore any trophies (though their weighting is always going to be a 
matter for debate).  Reflecting other approaches at a Clan level would 
be better done by adding new Clan trophies; Most Ascendingest is an 
obvious choice, as is Highest Scoring.

Oh, and several folks have made good arguments against a mandatory Grand 
Master category.  We still like the idea, but we'll probably offer it as 
a option for eligible players who choose it, but it will not be mandatory.

